WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:17.411
Crack! dove out of the way just as the lightning bolt struck a mailbox.

2
00:00:17.431 --> 00:00:21.294
"Whew!" Roxy took a deep breath.

3
00:00:21.314 --> 00:00:24.236
"That was a close—" Crack!

4
00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:26.378
Another bolt of lightning struck.

5
00:00:27.339 --> 00:00:28.660
Roxy jumped out of the way again.

6
00:00:31.448 --> 00:00:35.290
"You think you're so quick, Rocket Girl," shouted Weatherman.

7
00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:38.871
"I'd like to see you try to jump away from this!"

8
00:00:40.012 --> 00:00:42.012
Weatherman threw another Weather Ball into the air.

9
00:00:42.032 --> 00:00:44.473
"Weather Ball, activate!"

10
00:00:44.733 --> 00:00:45.334
he shouted.

11
00:00:48.355 --> 00:00:50.816
A strong wind blew, throwing Roxy off her feet.

12
00:00:52.517 --> 00:00:53.737
Rain began to pour down.

13
00:00:54.737 --> 00:00:55.958
Crack! Boom!

14
00:00:56.818 --> 00:00:57.759
More lightning struck.

15
00:00:58.659 --> 00:01:00.960
Roxy jumped to her feet, dodging bolts of lightning.

16
00:01:03.148 --> 00:01:05.049
"Listen, Weatherman," shouted Roxy.

17
00:01:05.069 --> 00:01:08.932
"Your dumb little thunderstorm isn't going to stop me!"

18
00:01:08.952 --> 00:01:12.374
"Maybe not," said Weatherman with a smirk.

19
00:01:12.394 --> 00:01:14.956
"But I have something that will."

20
00:01:16.177 --> 00:01:17.818
He threw another Weather Ball into the air.

21
00:01:17.838 --> 00:01:20.560
"Weather Ball, activate!"

22
00:01:22.141 --> 00:01:23.662
Roxy felt a change in the air.

23
00:01:24.563 --> 00:01:27.084
There was a rumbling sound, and the wind grew stronger.

24
00:01:27.104 --> 00:01:31.387
"Uh-oh. What's happening now?"

25
00:01:31.607 --> 00:01:32.308
Roxy wondered.

26
00:01:33.428 --> 00:01:38.652
And then she saw it—a huge tornado was whipping down West Street.

27
00:01:43.015 --> 00:01:44.956
Roxy screamed as she was swept upward.

28
00:01:46.598 --> 00:01:47.999
She spun around and around.

29
00:01:48.019 --> 00:01:51.021
"I'm getting dizzy!"

30
00:01:51.301 --> 00:01:51.821
she yelled.

31
00:01:53.182 --> 00:01:54.203
Roxy heard voices.

32
00:01:54.223 --> 00:01:57.005
"Help!" a woman shouted.

33
00:01:57.025 --> 00:01:58.826
"Rocket Girl!

34
00:01:58.906 --> 00:01:59.807
Save me!"

35
00:02:00.227 --> 00:02:00.948
shouted a man.

36
00:02:02.348 --> 00:02:05.450
The tornado had picked up a bus and a taxi along with Roxy.

37
00:02:06.731 --> 00:02:08.311
All the passengers were terrified.

38
00:02:09.232 --> 00:02:09.952
"Oh no!"

39
00:02:10.292 --> 00:02:10.953
Roxy thought.

40
00:02:10.973 --> 00:02:13.434
"I have to save those people!"

41
00:02:15.976 --> 00:02:18.657
Roxy used all her strength to fly around the tornado.

42
00:02:19.718 --> 00:02:21.419
She grabbed the taxi with one hand.

43
00:02:21.439 --> 00:02:26.622
"Grr!" Roxy grunted as she flew toward the bus.

44
00:02:26.642 --> 00:02:28.663
"Got it!"

45
00:02:28.863 --> 00:02:30.544
she shouted, grabbing hold of the bus.

46
00:02:34.285 --> 00:02:37.225
With her hands full, Roxy flew away from the tornado.

47
00:02:38.226 --> 00:02:40.146
She looked for a safe place to put the vehicles.

48
00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:44.307
As the tornado died down, the police came around a corner.

49
00:02:44.327 --> 00:02:46.208
"There's Weatherman!"

50
00:02:46.508 --> 00:02:47.708
shouted one police officer.

51
00:02:47.728 --> 00:02:49.949
"I need a blizzard!"

52
00:02:50.569 --> 00:02:53.190
Weatherman cried, throwing another Weather Ball into the air.

53
00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:56.170
The air grew colder.

54
00:02:56.911 --> 00:02:58.671
A few snowflakes began to fall down.

55
00:02:59.651 --> 00:03:01.492
Then a strong wind whipped along the street.

56
00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:05.201
The snow fell faster, and soon the street was covered.

57
00:03:06.082 --> 00:03:08.083
The police cars skidded through the deep snow.

58
00:03:08.903 --> 00:03:10.884
They slid off the street and onto the sidewalk.

59
00:03:14.326 --> 00:03:16.587
Weatherman got back into his van and pressed a button.

60
00:03:17.727 --> 00:03:20.649
The van's wheels folded in and were replaced with snow treads.

61
00:03:26.011 --> 00:03:27.512
Weatherman cackled and drove away.
